      "title": "Man in Swindon charged with assisting Russian intelligence agency",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/09/man-charged-with-assisting-russian-intelligence-agency-uk",
      "description": "<p>Joshua Cammidge, 31, arrested after investigation led by counter-terrorism policing London</p><p>A man has been charged with offences related to national security as part of an ongoing investigation led by counter-terrorism policing (CTP) London, according to the Metropolitan police.</p><p>Joshua Cammidge, 31, was arrested at an address in Swindon on Friday 4 September by CTP London officers, supported by officers from Wiltshire police. Searches were also carried out at a different address in Swindon. He was further arrested and detained the following day, being charged with assisting a foreign intelligence service and intending to commit or engage in conduct to prepare an act of sabotage.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/09/man-charged-with-assisting-russian-intelligence-agency-uk\">Continue reading...</a>",
